==Battleground==
*1 [[Metal Hippoe]] spawns.
*1 [[Metal Hippoe]] spawns after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.
*1 [[Metal Hippoe]] spawns after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>.
*1 [[Metal Hippoe]] spawns after 9 seconds<sup>270f</sup>.
*1 [[Metal Hippoe]] spawns after 14 seconds<sup>420f</sup>.
*8 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Box Witch and Minions]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Metal Doge]]s spawn, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
**8 [[Metal One Horn]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
**4 [[Super Metal Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 33.33~40 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The [[Metal Enemies|Metal]] Hippoes and Doges can be stalled with a freezing them with [[Hoopmaster Cat]], allowing as much time as needed to build up money or stack units. They could also be knockbacked with a unit like [[Quizmaster Cat]] to keep them alive and use them as stepping stones when the boss spawns, but this is often unnecessary and may be impossible on higher magnifications.

[[My Very Best Friend (Combo)]] and the units in it should be used to match the extreme magnifications with their own insane anti-Witch multipliers, especially on higher Crown levels, along with 2-3 [[Critical]] units and meatshields. Guaranteed Critters like [[Soba Cat]] are helpful to reduce the need to stack still helpful ones like [[Catasaurus]], when they are vulnerable due to the aggressive boss and [[Knockback]] on the Super Metal Hippoes. Even if not intentionally abusing the Metals as stepping stones, LD and [[:Category:Waver-class Cats|Wave]] units are still recommended to damage the boss.

